      ms: 5320
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||How willing he is to move spending between now and later, and whether he lends or borrows.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1kpkjtx'
    '|b||So ''save more'' is a claim about those two things, not a law. Let''s measure them.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6520
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1qjagdw'
    '|a||To see why, plan the fisher''s spending for thirty years, the way a permanent-income household would: set by lifetime resources, not this year''s pay.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9960
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||At two percent, the rate that matches his patience, the plan is flat: about twenty-six thousand a year.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:f4ugwy'
    '|b||Patience meaning what, exactly?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3040
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:4m2fko'
    '|a||A dollar next year is worth about two percent less to him than a dollar today. At two percent, waiting pays exactly what it costs him.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1p9nnap'
    '|a||Now one dial: how willing he is to move spending between years. Economists call it sigma, the elasticity of intertemporal substitution.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:17cha5x'
    '|a||Say sigma is two, very willing, and the rate rises to three percent, for good.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1cgwaix'
    '|a||Later has become cheaper, so he tilts his plan toward later, and today''s spending falls twelve percent. That''s the net of two forces. The one pulling down is the substitution effect: the ''save more'' advice.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 13280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:92m1p0'
    '|b||And the other force? His six hundred thousand now earns more interest. He''s richer.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4920
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:13vy7zo'
    '|a||That''s the income effect, pushing up: richer, he can spend more in every year, today included. At sigma two, substitution wins. At sigma one, the two cancel exactly: today doesn''t move, only the tilt does.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 15480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:x464ys'
    '|a||Now sigma is one half: he is less willing to shift. When the rate rises to 3%, what happens to his spending today?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:6gvala'
    '|a||It rises: with a weak pull toward later, the income effect wins.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4920
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||Six and a half percent more today, from a rate rise. For a saver who is reluctant to shift, the naive answer flips.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7840
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||Your turn: slide sigma and the rate, and find where the fisher''s response changes sign.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:dy6tbm'
    '|b||There''s one equation behind every one of these plans. Show the math, or skip it?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4560
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||The plan obeys one rule, the Euler equation: spending later over spending now equals delta times one plus r, all to the power sigma.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10160
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||Delta is patience. When delta times one plus r is one, waiting pays exactly what it costs, and the path is flat.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:102j30i'
    '|a||Raise r above the patience rate rho, and the path grows by about sigma times the gap: that''s substitution.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1ky3o24'
    '|a||The budget then sets the level of the whole path, and that''s where income and wealth effects come in.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:10sixyj'
    '|a||So for a lender, the sign hangs on sigma. Now switch to Ingrid, who borrows today.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6400
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Same twenty-six thousand a year at two percent. Her money just arrives later.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4840
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:u8dqf6'
    '|a||Raise the rate to three percent, sigma still a half, and her spending today falls eight percent.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:10gan5n'
    '|b||Substitution, as before. And the interest on what she owes goes up, so the income effect turns against her.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7080
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1e2ibhz'
    '|a||And a third push: the pay she is counting on is worth less in today''s money when the future is discounted at three percent. Call it the wealth effect.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1dkrbj5'
    '|a||All three point down. Sweep sigma from almost nothing to two, and she cuts every time: four percent at the bottom, twenty-four at the top.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:d1nbsz'
    '|a||Your turn: slide her savings from none to all, and find the household who doesn''t react at all.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1242g93'
    '|b||Wait, though. Central banks signal their moves months ahead. Rates rarely jump by surprise.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5520
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||Then a rational planner has already built the rise into her plan. Say Ingrid learns today that rates go to four percent in five years.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1b93s0i'
    '|a||She trims spending at once, to about twenty-three thousand, and when the rise arrives, nothing jumps.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:vudm37'
    '|a||If it comes as a surprise, she spends twenty-six thousand for five years, then cuts sharply.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:16olx3e'
    '|b||So spending moves when the news arrives, not when the rate does.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4040
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1jelo8c'
    '|a||Everything so far hung on one number, sigma. For a saver, below one a rate rise means more spending today; above one, less.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10160
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||So which is it for real people? Guess first. Where does the average published estimate of sigma lie? Click on the line.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7280
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1qkuzq6'
    '|a||Studies report about a half on average. Tomáš Havránek gathered 2,735 estimates from 169 published studies.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10440
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||And he found that researchers too often leave out estimates that come out negative or insignificant.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6800
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:15r9wpj'
    '|a||Correct for that, and household data on people who hold assets give about 0.3 to 0.4. Aggregate data give about zero, close to what Robert Hall found in 1988.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:xvkynn'
    '|b||Not everyone agrees. Jonathan Gruber used differences in how people''s interest is taxed and found about two.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6560
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1hi0hms'
    '|a||How sure are we? That sigma is below one for most people is mostly agreed; its exact size is contested.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:cj6abw'
    '|a||So the ''save more'' pull is weaker than the advice assumes: for borrowers a rise bites, and for savers it may barely matter.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1pp5wmk'
    '|a||Three new cases. A family with steady pay has a big variable-rate mortgage and no savings. The real rate rises unexpectedly, for good. What happens to their spending today?':
